# Cote100: extension, descent, formal algebraization, and reused sources.
I(639,100,[3,4,5],P100,'unproved claim','F est pleinement fidèle','For S locally noetherian, U open, S\u2216U of characteristicp, the functor A↦(A|U,A[p∞],comparison) is claimed fully faithful when U meets every connected component.','The comparison φ must be an isomorphism, as used in the proof; the first display’s mere arrow is not enough. The phrase U dense is a sufficient condition, not the exact hypothesis.')
C(655,639,'With S locally noetherian, U meeting every connected component and all points of S\u2216U of characteristicp, a compatible pair consisting of an abelian-scheme morphism on U and a p-divisible-group morphism on S is claimed to come from a unique morphism on S.','proof sketched','C','R-Q20/21: the manuscript points to Grothendieck1966 Thm1.2 for the algebraicity-locus step. Krishnamoorthy–Pál Cor6.12 verifies the normal-base extension setting; it does not alone establish the present broader connected-component formulation. The exact locus theorem is separately C-SA04-657.',['RGroth1966','RKP2021'],computation='Given a closed algebraicity locus which is open at characteristicp points, its restriction to U is all of U and it is open everywhere on its support; as a closed-and-open subset meeting every connected component it is S. The scheme-theoretic conclusion requires the universal closed-subscheme statement, not merely this topological argument.',confidence='medium')
I(640,100,[3,7,9,11,13,15],P100,'self-flagged step','une équivalence des catégories','Essential surjectivity is claimed after a finite geometrically-unibranch cover and étale-depth≥2 condition, with an alternative third-face closure condition on connected components.','These are the manuscript’s stronger descent hypotheses; normality is a different sufficient setting, not an equivalent reformulation. Cancelled intermediate conditions remain recorded.')
C(656,640,'Let S,U,p be as in C-SA04-655. Assume a finite surjection S′→S with S′ geometrically unibranch and prof_et_(S\u2216U)(S)≥2; the source claims every compatible abelian scheme on U and p-divisible group on S is effective. It also proposes replacing the depth condition by generation of π0(S′×S S′) from components meeting U under the third-face rule.','proof sketched','C','R-Q20/21/22 searched Grothendieck’s1966 paper, SGA7 references, deJong1998 and the later normal-base proof in KP2021. KP Cor6.12 proves extension iff the p-divisible group extends for normal locally noetherian X with dense U and characteristicp boundary; it does not prove the exact nonnormal simplicial criterion.',['RGroth1966','RKP2021','RdeJongICM1998'],confidence='medium',present='Normal-base case established; the exact finite-unibranch/third-face formulation remains a distinct unresolved bibliographic match, with effectivity gaps visible on the pages.')
I(641,100,[4,21],P100,'unproved claim','sous-schéma fermé','The algebraicity locus of one specified p-divisible-group homomorphism is asserted to be a universal closed subscheme, open near its characteristicp points.','This does not say every p-adic homomorphism is algebraic; the map is fixed throughout. Scan21 adds a maximal/associated-point specialization criterion.')
C(657,641,'For abelian schemes A,B over a locally noetherian S and a fixed u_p:A[p∞]→B[p∞], the source asserts a closed subscheme T representing base changes on which u_p is induced by an abelian-scheme homomorphism, and openness of T near its characteristicp points; it deduces a criterion using maximal and associated points.','proof sketched','A','R-Q20/23: the page explicitly cites Inventiones1.2, identified as Grothendieck1966. The primary article and its later citations were checked; the exact comparison is recorded in the source-verification appendix. The author’s later one-fibre algebraicity discussion must not be conflated with a full Tate-surjectivity assertion.',['RGroth1966','RGrothMumford1966'],confidence='medium',date='Published1966; the May9,1966 letter says the text is being written. Publisher nominal issue month is not used to infer actual first circulation.')
I(642,100,[15,17],P100,'withdrawn in the same text','Douteux, sans doute faux','The local-ring family gluing lemma is introduced and then explicitly doubted; full faithfulness is separately left to the reader.','Pointwise-compatible local schemes are not automatically an effective open-cover descent datum. The author’s doubt is retained, without inventing a counterexample.')
C(658,642,'The source claims full faithfulness of the functor from finite-type S-schemes to compatible systems over all local rings O_S,s, and uses it to glue the p-power torsion comparison.','stated without proof','C','R-Q22/24 searched local-ring systems, scheme descent and proper descent, then compared EGA finite-presentation localization and Rydh’s effective étale descent theorem. Those results do not by themselves verify this exact all-point system formulation.',['REGAIV4','RRydh2010'],confidence='medium',present='A precise compatibility category and a proof of uniform local spreading are required; no proof is imported from ordinary open-cover descent.')
C(659,642,'Every compatible local-ring system of abelian schemes is claimed to be globally effective, but the author marks the lemma doubtful and probably false.','corrected by himself later','D','R-Q22/24 searched the exact local-system phrase, abelian-scheme descent, Grothendieck1966 and later normal-base extension proofs. No exact published theorem supporting the unrestricted effectivity lemma was located. The on-page withdrawal is the strongest evidence of its fate; absence of a hit is not a novelty claim.',['RGroth1966','RKP2021','RRydh2010'],confidence='medium',present='Withdrawn/doubted in this text; not promoted to an open theorem without a fully specified category.')
I(643,100,[19],P100,'self-flagged step','∀ voisinage ouvert','The proposed neighborhood is chosen before all later choices of smaller V′, abelian B′/V′ and local isomorphism at t.','The quantifier order ∃V∀V′∀B′∀φ_t is stronger than the usual spreading statement for a fixed B′ and morphism. The source’s uniqueness sentence also reverses which components should be removed.')
C(660,643,'For fixed B/S and t, the source asks for one neighborhood V such that every abelian B′ on every t-neighborhood V′⊂V, with an isomorphism over SpecO_S,t, has that isomorphism uniquely over all V′.','open on the pages','D','R-Q24 searched the exact uniform-neighborhood/local-isomorphism formulation, EGA limit-spreading results and abelian Hom rigidity. The opened results spread one finite-presentation datum after a datum-dependent shrink; none supplies the source’s uniform ∃V∀B′ quantifier.',['REGAIV4','RKP2021'],confidence='medium',present='No exact theorem located; the uniform version should be isolated from the standard datum-dependent localization statement.')
I(644,100,[23,25],P100,'self-flagged step','épimorphisme propre','The author proves descent of maps to formally unramified targets along a proper schematic epimorphism, then invokes it for Hom of abelian schemes and asks for the p-divisible analogue.','A schematic epimorphism condition is stronger than bare surjectivity and must be retained. The argument for morphisms is not effectivity of descent of objects.')
C(661,644,'For a proper schematic epimorphism f:S′→S of locally noetherian schemes and a formally unramified S-scheme X, the displayed equalizer condition on maps from S′ and S′×S S′ is asserted to descend to S.','proof sketched','C','R-Q22/25 compared the source’s algebra equalizer/radicial reduction with Rydh2010 Thms5.17/5.21. Rydh proves effective descent in the étale category under universal subtrusiveness; that is related but not the same formally-unramified-target theorem as written here.',['RRydh2010'],confidence='medium',present='The schematic and infinitesimal hypotheses are indispensable; no blanket descent claim for every proper surjection is recorded.')
C(662,644,'The Hom functor of p-divisible groups should be formally unramified, so that the same rigidity/descent mechanism applies; the manuscript leaves this verification open.','open on the pages','B','R-Q19/25: the Grothendieck–Messing deformation description makes lifts of BT morphisms unique when they exist, with the filtration condition controlling existence. DeJong1998 supplies generic-Hom extension over normal domains, which is a different assertion.',['RMazurMessing1974','RdeJongICM1998'],confidence='medium',present='Rigidity is part of the standard deformation theory in its nilpotent divided-power setting; the source’s unrestricted base/topology formulation must be matched to that setting.')
